---
import { getVersionedDocsPath } from '@libs/path.ts'

interface Props {
  /**
   * The name of the component which disabled state is being described.
   */
  name?: string
}

const { name } = Astro.props
---

<p>Make { name } inactive by adding the <code>[disabled]</code> boolean attribute to the <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> element. Disabled { name } have <code>pointer-events: none</code> applied to them, preventing hover and active states from triggering.</p>

<slot name="buttonExample" />

<p>Disabled { name } using the <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> element behave a bit different:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Disabled { name } using <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> must include the <code>aria-disabled="true"</code> attribute to indicate the state of the element to assistive technologies, to make it visually appear disabled and disable all <code>pointer-events</code>.</li>
  <li>Disabled { name } using <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> <em>should not</em> include the <code>href</code> attribute. In case you need to keep the <code>href</code>, please refer to <a href={getVersionedDocsPath('/components/links#disabled-link-accessibility-warning')}>disabled link accessibility warning</a>.</li>
</ul>

<slot name="anchorExample" />
